{"content":[{"c":["TISHBE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Native city of Elijah the prophet and its inhabitants (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.17.1","r":"1Kgs.17.1","rawR":"1Kgs.17.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.17.1","value":"1Kgs.17.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 17:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.21.17,28","r":"1Kgs.21.17,28","rawR":"1Kgs.21.17,28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.21.17,28","value":"1Kgs.21.17,28"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:17, 28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.1.3,8","r":"2Kgs.1.3,8","rawR":"2Kgs.1.3,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.1.3,8","value":"2Kgs.1.3,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 1:3, 8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.9.36","r":"2Kgs.9.36","rawR":"2Kgs.9.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.9.36","value":"2Kgs.9.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:36"},"). The Hebrew form of Tishbe in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.17.1","r":"1Kgs.17.1","rawR":"1Kgs.17.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.17.1","value":"1Kgs.17.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kings 17:1"}," prompted the KJV to translate the word as “of the inhabitants [of Gilead].” Most translations follow the Septuagint, however, in considering Tishbe a proper noun. This reading is also supported by the fact that Elijah is elsewhere called a Tishbite. If Tishbe is considered a proper name, it is likely identified with Thisbe, a town in Naphtali that is mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Tb.1.2","r":"Tb.1.2","rawR":"Tb.1.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Tb.1.2","value":"Tb.1.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Tobit 1:2"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tishbe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 17:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.17.1","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.17.1","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.17.1"},{"anchorText":"21:17, 28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.21.17,28","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.21.17,28","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.21.17,28"}